                "message": "✨ Make batch jobs stoppable with C-g and visible from outside Emacs\n\n- Timers run with inhibit-quit set, so C-g never reached a batch job; a slice now lets it through and stops the job.\n- Two C-g in a row stop the jobs; M-x sp-batch-cancel and k in the report buffer too.\n- Running jobs leave a status file in var/batch-jobs; M-x sp-batch-list-jobs and tools/sp-batch-jobs list and stop them from another Emacs or a shell.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiBhjMEvTpuoTULaVya",
